      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "During World War II the Big Inch pipeline ran through Norris City, moving oil from Texas to the Northeast and easing Atlantic tanker losses.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        23,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norris_City%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Village officials say small‑town values, guided growth, and heritage preservation are core principles that make Norris City a wonderful place to call home.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.villageofnorriscity.com/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Norris City was officially incorporated as a village in 1901, solidifying its status after decades of railroad‑driven growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norris_City%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The original plat of Norris City was filed at the White County Courthouse in Carmi on August 17 1871, marking its formal layout.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norris_City%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "A post office opened in Norris City on May 15 1871, serving residents long before the town’s official platting.",
